<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Combat Extended support for the Drachenjaeger's turrets.

  This file lives in the VEHICLES folder, which is gated on Vehicle Framework, and
  is itself guarded by PatchOperationFindMod on Combat Extended. So it applies only
  when BOTH are active, and does nothing otherwise. It is NOT in
  1.6/Mods/CombatExtended, because that folder is gated on CE alone and these
  xpaths would then target defs that do not exist.

  WHY IT IS NEEDED

  Decompiling Vehicles.VehicleTurret shows the fire path forks:

      if (LaunchProjectileCE == null)
          val3 = (Projectile)GenSpawn.Spawn(projectileDef, ...);   // vanilla
      ...
      LaunchProjectileCE(projectileDef, loadedAmmo, modExtension?._ammoSet, ...)

  With CE loaded the framework takes the CE branch and hands it the ammo set from
  a CETurretDataDefModExtension. With no such extension the projectile is a plain
  vanilla bullet being pushed through CE's launcher, which throws

      InvalidCastException: Specified cast is not valid

  every time the turret fires - reported in game as "Exception thrown while
  shooting turret ... Removing from queue to resolve issue temporarily."

  Nothing catches this at load: the defs are all valid, and the fault only appears
  the first time somebody pulls the trigger.

  PATTERN taken verbatim from Combat Extended's own vehicle patches, which use
  PatchOperationAddModExtension for exactly this - see its ModPatches folder,
  Alpha Vehicles / Age of Sail / Alpha_FrigateShip_Turret.xml.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Combat Extended</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!--
          Particle battery: a charged-shot autocannon in CE terms. 20x105mmCharged
          is CE's own charged autocannon set, so the ballistics and armour maths
          come from CE rather than from numbers invented here.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleTurretDef[defName="RR_Drachenjager_ParticleCannon"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <li Class="Vehicles.CETurretDataDefModExtension">
              <ammoSet>AmmoSet_20x105mmCharged</ammoSet>
              <!-- It stands forty metres. The muzzle is a long way up. -->
              <shotHeight>6.5</shotHeight>
              <speed>140</speed>
              <sway>0.55</sway>
              <spread>0.09</spread>
            </li>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleTurretDef[defName="RR_Drachenjager_WarheadRack"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <li Class="Vehicles.CETurretDataDefModExtension">
              <!--
                AmmoSet_120mmCannonShell, deliberately, and NOT AmmoSet_40mmRocket
                which reads like the better thematic fit. That one is defined in
                CE's ModPatches/Rimsenal Enhanced Vanilla folder, so it only exists
                for players who also run Rimsenal - this patch would resolve to
                nothing for everyone else and fail exactly the way it does now.
                Only ammo sets from CE's own Defs/ tree are safe to name.
              -->
              <ammoSet>AmmoSet_120mmCannonShell</ammoSet>
              <shotHeight>7.0</shotHeight>
              <speed>55</speed>
              <sway>1.20</sway>
              <spread>0.30</spread>
            </li>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
